- op: discuss  # 5f1e
  at: '2026-08-28T22:43:12Z'  # 5f1e
  by: agent  # 5f1e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5f1e
  clock: 3  # 5f1e
  nonce: 5f1e  # 5f1e
  message: "INVESTIGATED. THIS ITEM'S MECHANISM IS WRONG AND ITS POPULATION IS 11 ROWS, NOT\n3. Write-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/zumoz_probe_08282026/RESULT.md\nRoot cause filed as INV-misup (violated, P2), which now BLOCKS this item.\n\n(1) THE CATALOGUE SIDE MATCHES THEM FINE. Feeding well-formed synthetic edges to\nclassify_call: WebSocket.onmessage, WebSocket.onclose and EventSource.onmessage\nALL match -- with construct \"method\", with construct \"assignment\", and with no\nconstruct meta at all. So \"a method-keyed row can never match, because assignment\nis not a call\" is NOT what is happening. The row is matchable; the edge is what\nis missing.\n\n(2) THE ANALYZER EMITS NO EDGE FOR ANY CONSTRUCTOR-STYLE BROWSER GLOBAL. Four\nfixtures through io-boundaries, fresh cache each, with two positive controls\nfiring in the same runs:\n    fetch(...)                     function-keyed global    MATCHED (control)\n    localStorage.setItem/getItem   method on NAMED global   MATCHED (control)\n    x.open/x.send  x = new XMLHttpRequest()                 no chain\n    ws.send(...)   ws = new WebSocket(...)  module scope    no chain\n    ws.addEventListener('message', cb)  A REAL METHOD CALL  no chain\n    ws.onmessage = cb              property assignment      no chain\n    TypeScript: const ws: WebSocket = new WebSocket(...); ws.send(...)  no chain\nTHE DISCRIMINATOR IS RECEIVER SHAPE, NOT ASSIGNMENT-VS-CALL: a named-global\nreceiver resolves, a `new`-constructed instance never does.\n\n(3) SO TWO CLAIMS IN THIS ITEM ARE FALSE AS WRITTEN:\n  * \"addEventListener does match, so the surface is addEventListener-only\" --\n    addEventListener is EQUALLY unreachable. The WebSocket/SSE receive surface\n    is not thinner than the catalogue suggests, it is EMPTY.\n  * \"three dead rows\" -- it is eleven: WebSocket.{addEventListener, onclose,\n    onmessage, send}, EventSource.{addEventListener, onmessage},\n    XMLHttpRequest.{open, send, setRequestHeader},\n    BroadcastChannel.{addEventListener, postMessage}.\n  The PR #606 justification this item corrects is still corrected, just not for\n  the stated reason: onmessage does not carry the receive because NOTHING on\n  WebSocket does.\n\n(4) REACHES INTO WI-lunav. XMLHttpRequest.open is one of that item's eight\nbuilder rows and is unreachable, so no finding could ever have existed at that\nrow to adjudicate -- a silent zero that would have read as \"nothing wrong here\".\n\n(5) OPTION (a) IS NOW THE WRONG MOVE, on a reason this item could not have had.\nAn inert row has ZERO precision cost, so deleting it buys no precision; and\nthere is no false-COVERAGE risk either, because a call that never classifies is\nnever counted as EXAMINED (INV-buzab) and javascript's catalogue status is\n`in_progress`, so it claims no module_completeness. What the rows DO carry is\nthe specification of what should match once the receiver-typing gap closes.\nDeleting 11 correct rows to describe an analyzer limitation puts the defect in\nthe wrong artifact.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: keep the rows, pin the inertness so it cannot change silently,\nand fix INV-misup -- which is recall-ADDING and therefore band-stopped under\nWI-sivuz. This item is BLOCKED on that, on evidence rather than on the guess in\nits option (b). No catalogue change shipped."  # 5f1e
